<title>USA: U.S. Senator calls for aggressive EEP subsidies.</title>
<headline>U.S. Senator calls for aggressive EEP subsidies.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Sen. Byron Dorgan, D-ND, said he wrote to Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman on Tuesday asking him to use grain export subsidies aggressively against the European Union.</p>
<p>&quot;This nation must send a clear message that it will not stand by while others seek to expand their market share at the expense of American producers,&quot; Dorgan said.</p>
<p>Dorgan said in a statement that prices had dropped by a third from their peak earlier this year, in the face of &quot;intense subsidized competition from the European Union&quot; and other exporters.</p>
<p>Glickman has said the Agriculture Department will use Export Enhancement Program subsidies if necessary to defend U.S. markets.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
</text>
